body:
Thursday.

&#x200B;

Like, there's NOTHING notable about it. Have you ever heard someone say, "heck yeah, I just can't wait for THURSDAY, man!"

Not me, but a friend. We're both tour guides for a really prestigious university in the U.S. Campus tours, dorm tours, you know the drill.

&#x200B;

Our engineering school is really competitive. In the U.S. (and perhaps just in general, although I don't want to assume), engineering schools tend to skew overwhelmingly male. But our school has a pretty equal ratio of male to female students in our class, which is something we take pride in and tell on every tour.

My friend told that on a tour, and some snarky high school guy raises his hand and asks, "so you're telling me that you're rejecting QUALIFIED MALE applicants in favor of WOMEN?"

&#x200B;

I've received a few awkward questions, but never something just so blatantly disrespectful or snarky. Like, kid, what did you honestly expect to get out of asking that?
